.TH GI-AI 1 "2026" "gi-ai 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gi, gi-ai \- Ĝi, a private local AI assistant
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gi
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR ...
.br
.B gi ask
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR] \fIQUESTION\fR
.br
.B gi \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Ĝi answers questions with a language model that runs on this computer
(Ollama or LM Studio) and keeps a private workspace of task records.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B health
Check Ĝi and the model server. Exit 0 when the server gives a valid reply,
1 when it does not, 2 on a configuration error. The report shows the endpoint
that was used. With the lmstudio backend the model counts as available only
when the server lists \fBllm.model\fR exactly; the report then adds whether it
is loaded, its capabilities, the server version and the names (never the
values) of reply fields Ĝi does not know.
.TP
.BI "ask " QUESTION
Ask the model a question. With \fB\-\-verbose\fR, one line with the reply
statistics (tokens in and out, reasoning tokens, tokens per second, time to
first token) is printed to standard error after the answer, or
\fBstats: none\fR when the server sends none. The question is passed to the
model between two marker lines; marker text inside the question
(\fB<<<QUESTION\fR or \fBQUESTION>>>\fR, in any letter case) is replaced by
\fB[marker removed]\fR. The length limit applies to the question as typed.
.TP
.B init-workspace \fR[\fB\-\-path\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Create the private workspace (mode 0700) with a hash-chained audit log.
.TP
.B task new \-\-type \fR{req,bug,vuln} \fB\-\-title \fITEXT\fR
Create a task record. \fBtask list\fR lists them.
.TP
.B selfcheck
Check the local security baseline: private workspace (\fBworkspace-private\fR),
intact audit log (\fBaudit-chain\fR), config files not world-writable,
\fBmodel-endpoint-private\fR (the endpoint is loopback, or a private, link-local
or shared address when \fBllm.allow_remote\fR is true) and, when a token file is
set, \fBtoken-file-private\fR (owned by you, no group or other permissions).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Keys in the \fB[llm]\fR table:
.TP
.B backend
\fBollama\fR (default), \fBlmstudio\fR or \fBecho\fR (offline, repeats the question).
.TP
.B endpoint
\fBhttp://\fIhost\fR[\fB:\fIport\fR] or https; no user, path or query.
The host \fB@gateway\fR is replaced on every run by the IPv4 default-route
gateway read from /proc/net/route (for LM Studio on the Windows host of WSL).
Any host that is not loopback, including \fB@gateway\fR, needs
\fBallow_remote = true\fR.
.TP
.B model\fR, \fBtimeout_s\fR (1-3600), \fBallow_remote
Model name, request timeout in seconds, and whether a non-local endpoint is allowed.
.TP
.B reasoning
lmstudio only: \fBoff\fR (default), \fBlow\fR, \fBmedium\fR, \fBhigh\fR,
\fBon\fR, or \fBdefault\fR to send nothing and keep the model's own default.
.TP
.B context_length\fR (256-1048576), \fBmax_output_tokens\fR (1-131072), \fBtemperature\fR (0-1)
lmstudio only; sent only when set.
.TP
.B token_file
a file holding the API token, sent by the lmstudio backend only. It must
be inside \fI~/.config/gi\-ai/\fR (this place does not follow
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR); any other place is a configuration error and the file
is not opened. This place is checked whatever the backend, also when
\fBGI_AI_LLM_TOKEN\fR is set. The file itself must not be a symbolic link, and
a symbolically linked folder that leads out of \fI~/.config/gi\-ai/\fR is
refused. When the file is used, it must be owned by you with mode 0600 or
stricter, or every command stops with a configuration error. A token cannot
be written in a config file.
.IP
A token, from this file or from \fBGI_AI_LLM_TOKEN\fR, is only sent to an
endpoint whose host is a loopback address or a private, link-local or shared
address (the addresses \fBmodel-endpoint-private\fR accepts). With a token set
and any other host (a public address or a name other than \fBlocalhost\fR),
every command stops with the configuration error
\fBrefusing to send the API token to\fR \fIhost\fR\fB: not a local or private address\fR
before any connection is made.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GI_AI_LLM_TOKEN
API token for the lmstudio backend. When set and not empty it wins over
\fBllm.token_file\fR. It is sent only in the Authorization header to the
configured endpoint and is never printed or stored. The same address rule as
for \fBllm.token_file\fR applies: with a public address or a host name other
than \fBlocalhost\fR as the endpoint, every command stops with a configuration
error.
.TP
.B GI_AI_CONFIG
An extra config file read after the user config.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_DATA_HOME
Base directories for the user config and the workspace.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/gi-ai/gi.toml
System defaults.
.TP
.I ~/.config/gi-ai/gi.toml
Your settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gi-ai/workspace
Your private workspace.
.TP
.I /proc/net/route
Read only when the endpoint uses \fB@gateway\fR.
.TP
.I llm.token_file
The API token file you name in the settings, if any (mode 0600, inside
\fI~/.config/gi\-ai/\fR).
.SH SECURITY
Ĝi treats model output as untrusted and removes terminal control sequences
before printing it, including error texts from the model server. Ĝi never
reads hidden files or upper-case Markdown files (such as instruction files
written for other AI tools) as content. Ĝi connects only to the configured
endpoint: proxy settings are ignored and redirects are not followed. LM Studio
chats are stateless, Ĝi sends no tools, and a reply that calls a tool is
refused. Reasoning text from the model is never printed.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report bugs to \fBbugs@gi\-ai.app\fR.
Report security problems only through
.UR https://github.com/VadimBley/gi-ai/security/advisories/new
.UE ,
never by email.
